  "question": {
    "text": "A point source of light of power <math><msub><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> is placed at a distance of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> from the centre of a thin hemispherical shell as shown in the figure, The shell has a radius of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and it behaves like a perfect black body.&nbsp;If the temperature of the hemisphere is related to the power of the source as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>π</mi><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>' where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>σ</mi></math>&nbsp;is the Stefan's constant, then find the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math>.&nbsp;\r\r<p>&nbsp;</p>\r"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "27",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0074_f72fa6e952bb.png\" style=\"height: 167px; width: 170px;\" /><br /><br />Total power emitted by shell due to radiation<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>&#963;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#963;</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></math><br />Power gained by the shell from <math><msub><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> :<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mn>37</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math><br />Equating: <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&#963;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />Gives <math><msup><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>270</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>&#963;</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>270</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn></math></p>"
  }
